{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559523-advantages-traits","id":1559523,"title":"Advantages traits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-19T08:10:46-07:00","id":1559523,"title":"Advantages traits","content":"Can Mages start the games with Advantages traits without them coming from Biomods?<br /> For example, could a character start with armored skin and fangs because in their backstory they were once a ghoul fleshcrafted by a Tzimisce, or could a mage buy an alternate form with the Shapechanger Advantage because they're a Kinain with Pookah parent or their Totem gave it to them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-20T06:29:33-07:00","id":1559533,"title":"","content":"In general those things are best left to with Merits &amp; Flaws when possible<br /> <br /> I think it's OK, tho, if the ST allows it. It has the problem of the disadvantages that come with the Background, that are supposed to be caused by Paradox (that such powers wouldn't normally suffer). But the ST and player could find another explanation of why &quot;genetic flaws&quot; happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-20T09:45:50-07:00","id":1559534,"title":"","content":"Biomods are well within Mage purview. Technocracy Reloaded and the Progenitor Convention books have examples, but they cause permanent Paradox. As to mixing stuff from other splats... totally up to the Storyteller. I might allow the Tzimisce fleshcrafting, but there would big detriments. Tzimisce don't go for aesthetics most would appreciate. I would also warn the player that Tzimisce history would be a ST tool for unpleasant (but not unfun) future storyhooks. Fae magic and Sphere magic don't go together, so i would not let a player start with that, unless there was some powerful magic that had crossed the streams.<br /> Essentially, my gut reaction is usually, &quot;no, stay within the game&quot; unless there is a particularly good story to be had from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","name":"Heilong","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T03:47:24-07:00","id":1561458,"title":"","content":"Depending on your ST, you always have the option of directly buying those things from the patent gameline. Some cost XP, some cost a tradeoff, but most can be acquired in a quite straightforward manner.<br /> <br /> Some Merits or Backgrounds also cover either relationship or kinship to a supernatural. They are a good place to start to design a Merit for the desired effect, or just get the responsible party to be in your sheet.<br /> <br /> Merits are the best choice because they aren't Magic, and that's exactly what they represent in Mage in many cases: Paradox-free effects your character got simply because the world is that strange place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heilong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559523-advantages-traits?p=1559534#post1559534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fae magic and Sphere magic don't go together, so i would not let a player start with that, unless there was some powerful magic that had crossed the streams.</div> </div> </div> </div>I beg your pardon, but where did that came from? I don't remember any of the books that have ever said that. And I may not have read all of them, but I know both lines fairly well, and if I missed something I must know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}